                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} EL(\phi)\delta\phi = P(\phi)\lambda''(\phi)
            %p
          %h3#ViaPoissonStructure (P) Via Poisson structures
          %p
            The covariant phase space can be embedded into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+field+configurations"} space of field configurations
            as a subspace of the set of solutions that transversely intersects
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+orbit"} gauge orbit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+locus"} zero locus
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            and some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixing
            conditions. The non-degenerate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+structure"} Poisson structure
            on the algebra of functions on the covariant phase space is given by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peierls+bracket"} Peierls bracket
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peierls+bracket"} Peierls bracket
            of two functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is the antisymmetrized influence on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            of an infinitesimal perturbation of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge-fixed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            by function that restricts to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            on the embedding. The algebra of functions on the space of field configurations becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+algebra"} Poisson algebra
            in the following way. Pick a set of functions on the space of field configurations that restrict to a non-degenerate coordinate system on the embedded covariant phase space. These functions, together with the equations of motion and gauge fixing conditions define a Poisson bivector by being declared canonical, such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
            of the bivector coincides with the ideal generated by the equations of motion and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixing
            conditions. Obviously the Poisson structure thus constructed on the algebra of functions on field configurations is not unique and depends on the above choice of coordinates; the same non-uniqueness may be parametrized instead by a choice of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            on the space of field configurations. The embedded covariant phase space becomes a leaf of the symplectic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation"} foliation
            of the space of field configurations.
          %h3#ReducedCovariantPhaseSpaceViaBV Via the BV-complex
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+action+functional"} local action functional
            is (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} formal dual
            to) a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
            of the
            %em reduced
            covariant phase space (the quotient of the covariant phase space by symmetries). As discussed in more detail at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
            the ghost sector of that complex is a model for the quotient by the symmetries, whereas the antifield/antighost sector is a model for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/critical+locus"} critical locus
            of the action functional.
          %p
            Moreover, by the nature of its construction, the BV-complex is canonically equipped with a
            %em graded
            symplectic form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gerstenhaber+algebra"} (-1)-graded Poisson bracket
            is called the
            %em antibracket
            (essentially the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schouten+bracket"} Schouten bracket
            on graded derivations, see at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/derived+critical+locus"} derived critical locus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_\Sigma \omega
            on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+phase+space"} reduced phase space
          %p We want to claim the following
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+action+functional"} local action functional
              on a space of fields over a spacetime
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi BV
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{BV}
              denote the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              denote the horizontal de Rham differential on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi BV
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi Σ
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi X
                    %mi d
                    %mi ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{BV} \int_\Sigma \Omega = \int_X d \omega
                    \\,.
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globally+hyperbolic+spacetime"} globally hyperbolic spacetime
              of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \times [0,1]
              then this is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi BV
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi Σ
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Σ
                          %mi out
                    %mi ω
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Σ
                          %mi in
                    %mi ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{BV} \int_\Sigma \Omega
                    \=
                    \\int_{\Sigma_{out}} \omega
                    \-
                    \\int_{\Sigma_{in}} \omega
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
            We discuss this now in more detail. (The stament then also appears in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#CattaneoMnevReshetikhin12"} Cattaneo-Mnev-Reshetikhin 12, equation (9)
          %p Write
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                on which the fields are defined;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Conf
                      %mo =
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Conf = Maps(X,V) = \Gamma_X(X \times V)
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} configuration space
                of fields on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                is some
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                (for simplicity);
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Conf
                        %mi BV
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Conf_{BV}
                for the BV-extension;
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi BV
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{BV}
                for the corresponding
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{v_a\}
                for a chosen
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi BV
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{BV}
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Φ
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mrow
                          %mi loc
                          %mo ,
                          %mi BV
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi Conf
                        %mi BV
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi^a(x) \in \Omega_{loc,BV}^{0,0}(X \times Conf_{BV})
                for the functional whose value on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Conf
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^a v_a \in Conf
                is
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^a(x)
                (for
                = succeed ");" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mrow
                          %mi loc
                          %mo ,
                          %mi BV
                        %mrow
                          %mo •
                          %mo ,
                          %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi Conf
                        %mi BV
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{loc,BV}^{\bullet,\bullet}(X \times Conf_{BV})
                for the corresponding
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+bicomplex"} variational bicomplex
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi Φ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi loc
                        %mrow
                          %mi dim
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi Conf
                        %mi BV
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar \Phi_a(x) \in \Omega^{dim X,0}_{loc}(X \times Conf_{BV})
                for the antifield corresponding to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Φ
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi^a(x)
                (which is an
                %em antighost
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Φ
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi^a(x)
                is a ghost).
          %p
            Then the symplectic form density
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            for the antibracket
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi loc
                      %mo ,
                      %mi BV
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi Conf
                    %mi BV
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega \in \Omega^{(n,2)}_{loc, BV}(X \times Conf_{BV})
          %p is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi var
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi Φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi var
                  %msup
                    %mi Φ
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega = \int_X d_{var} \bar \Phi_a(x) \wedge d_{var} \Phi^a(x)
                  \\,.
          %p Then,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi BV
                          %msub
                            %mo ∫
                            %mi Σ
                          %mi Ω
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi BV
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msub
                              %mo ∫
                              %mi Σ
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mi var
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi Φ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                              %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∧
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mi var
                            %msup
                              %mi Φ
                              %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi var
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi BV
                          %msub
                            %mo ∫
                            %mi Σ
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi Φ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                            %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∧
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi var
                          %msup
                            %mi Φ
                            %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  d_{BV} \int_\Sigma \Omega
                  \&amp; =
                  d_{BV} \left(
                  \\int_\Sigma
                  d_{var} \bar \Phi_a(x) \wedge d_{var} \Phi^a(x)
                  \\right)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; =
                  \- d_{var} (d_{BV} \int_\Sigma \bar \Phi_a(x)) \wedge d_{var} \Phi^a(x)
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            We observe that the term in parenthesis is – in the notation at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/derived+critical+locus"} derived critical locus
            (so we are assuming now the assumptions made there) –
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mover
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi BRST
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi BRST
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mover
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi BRST
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\hat S + d_{BRST}, d_{W(BRST)}]
                  \=
                  [\hat S, d_{W(BRST)}]
                  \\,.
          %p Hence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ⋯
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi var
                          %msub
                            %mi EL
                            %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∧
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi var
                          %msup
                            %mi Φ
                            %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mo ∫
                            %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi var
                          %mi EL
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\cdots &amp; =
                  \- d_{var} EL_a(x) \wedge d_{var} \Phi^a(x)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = - \int_X d_{var}  EL
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi EL
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi loc
                      %mo ,
                      %mi BV
                    %mrow
                      %mi dim
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Conf
                    %mi BV
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} EL \in \Omega^{dim X, 1}_{loc, BV}(X \times \mathrm{Conf}_{BV})
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equation"} Euler-Lagrange density
            as in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Zuckerman"} Zuckerman, p. 267
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %mi d
                  %mi ω
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots = - \int_X d \omega
                  \\,.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#relativistic_particle Relativistic particle
          %p
            The covariant phase space of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativistic+particle"} relativistic particle
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+manifold"} pseudo-Riemannian manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the space of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesic"} geodesic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (in the absence of a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+gauge+field"} background gauge field
          %h3#chernsimons_theory Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            corresponding to a non-degenerate bilienear
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -,-\rangle
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            the
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                configuration space is the space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1(\Sigma, \mathfrak{g})
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+valued+forms"} Lie algebra valued forms
            %li
              %p
                covariant phase space is the space of field configurations
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                whose
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
                2-form vanishes
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      F_A = 0
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+structure"} presymplectic structure
                is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi δ
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi δ
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Σ
                            %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi δ
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi δ
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\Omega(\delta A_1, \delta A_2) =
                      \\int_{\Sigma_0} \langle \delta A_1 \wedge \delta A_2\rangle
                      \\,.
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            for more details.
          %h3#in_dggeometry In dg-geometry
          %p (…)
          %p
            Let the ambient context be that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-geometry"} dg-geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be an ordinary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
